# How to cite this software. GitHub reads this file and offers a "Cite this
# repository" button from it; `cffconvert` turns it into BibTeX.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Onset Review: traceable analysis of high-frequency oscillations and seizure onset in intracranial EEG"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python library and desktop application for intracranial EEG.
  It detects ripples and fast ripples with four detectors and interictal
  discharges with a fifth, rejects filter ringing by testing each event against
  its spectral background, attaches an exact Poisson confidence interval to
  every channel rate and reports channels whose intervals overlap the leader's
  as a tied set, computes the Epileptogenicity Index of seizure onset, and
  records a reader's event-by-event review. An optional assistant answers
  questions about a saved analysis with a locally run open-weight model, under
  checks on its citations and numbers. Validated on OpenNeuro ds003498,
  ds003029 and ds004100. Research software: not a medical device, and not
  validated for clinical use.
type: software
authors:
